- Also, rrset.addRR(r) may throw exception if r is not of same type as RRset? But they already matched rtype. However if rrset already contains records of different type due to misuse, addRR may throw IllegalArgumentException. Not sure.

- The withWriteLock method may throw RuntimeException if lock acquisition fails? Not typical.

- The method may throw ClassCastException when casting r to SOARecord if actualType == Type.SOA but r is not instance of SOARecord (unlikely because Type.SOA ensures). But maybe subclass? Not needed.

