2. Adding SOA when existing RRset present but zone's soaRecord is null leads to NullPointerException from rrset.deleteRR(null). Expect NullPointerException or IllegalArgumentException depending on RRset implementation. We'll assume NullPointerException.

3. Possibly adding a record with mismatched RRset type (i.e., rtype not equal to type of existing RRset). But findRRsetWithoutLock uses rtype; if existing RRset of same name but different type, findRRsetWithoutLock(name, rtype) will return null (since type mismatch). So new RRset created; no exception.

